  "term": "pilocarpine",
  "definition": "Pilocarpine is a salivary stimulant used to treat intractable xerostomia, meaning ongoing dry mouth with reduced salivary gland function. In the source, it is described as commonly prescribed for this problem, though higher doses may cause more side effects and lower doses may be less effective.",
